   "summary": "<p>What the suite is built on, and the reason it is a <em>standalone</em> suite rather than a part of ForShor's order-finding development: it uses ForShor's gate language <code>LowGate</code>, its semantics classes (<code>QSemantics</code>, <code>LowerGateClass</code>), its resource model <code>shorGateResourceModel</code> (Cuccaro adders, arbitrary-angle rotations, not T), its basis-level gate laws, the naive-leaf lemmas and the pure master theorem. Nothing in ForShor imports it.</p><p>Imported (read from the sources): <code>ShorVerification.Framework.Gatecount.ResourceModel</code>, <code>ShorVerification.Implementation.PhaseProduct.Proofs.GateLaws</code>, <code>ShorVerification.Implementation.PhaseProduct.Proofs.Math.MasterTheorem</code>, <code>ShorVerification.Implementation.PhaseProduct.Proofs.NaiveLeaf</code>, <code>ShorVerification.Implementation.PhaseProduct.Proofs.Registers</code>, <code>ShorVerification.Model.Standard.Lift</code>, <code>ShorVerification.Model.Standard.LowGates</code>, <code>ShorVerification.Submission.Audit</code>.</p>",
