     "file": "PTP/Semantics.lean",
     "line": 55,
     "code": "/-- Exact PTP semantics. -/\ndef evalPhase (P : PTPPolicy) (n : Nat) (φ : ℚ) (x : Fin 3 → ℤ) : ℚ :=\n  match P.choose n with\n  | none => φ * x 0 * x 1 * x 2\n  | some T =>\n      if _h : childWidth n T.ops < n then\n        ∑ t : Fin T.pts.length,\n          P.evalPhase (childWidth n T.ops) (φ * T.coeff n t)\n            (fun s => (T.children id n (x s)).getD t 0)\n      else φ * x 0 * x 1 * x 2\ntermination_by n",
     "note": "The exact semantics of a policy: split, take \\(3k-2\\) smaller phases on the point values, recurse; or the plain product when no table applies or the width would not shrink."
