   "summary": "<p class=\"lmeta\">4 modules · 120 declarations · 1,860 lines</p><p>From one node to a whole policy. <code>SplitLayout</code> splits three parent registers in place into child slots (zero-extending lower limbs, sign-extending the top), <code>SpecOn</code> is the register-level phase contract with explicit workspace, and <code>PolicyImpl</code> is the recursion. Correctness and the census hold at every depth (<code>Recursion</code>), exist for every checked policy and width (<code>Build</code>), and include CNOT and And† counts and a qubit bound (<code>CensusFull</code>).</p><p>Widths here are the conservative scan.</p><table class=\"ptp-mods\"><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/Census.lean\">Census.lean</a></td><td>38 decls</td><td>PTP gate census and qubit layout, from the gate-level lowering</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/Recursion.lean\">Recursion.lean</a></td><td>46 decls</td><td>O2: a PTP node meets the child contract, so gate-level correctness recurses</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/Build.lean\">Build.lean</a></td><td>23 decls</td><td>O2 closed: every checked PTP policy has a gate-level recursion at every width</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/CensusFull.lean\">CensusFull.lean</a></td><td>13 decls</td><td>The rest of the census through the full recursion: And† and CNOT</td></tr></table>",
