   "summary": "<p class=\"lmeta\">2 modules · 12 declarations · 163 lines</p><p>The claim a reader should check, stated apart from the proof. The specification operator is a structure the reader supplies, so the statement does not mention <code>LowGate</code>. The theorem covers the linear span of <em>clean</em> basis kets: operands fit signed \\(n\\ge1\\) bits and the workspace is \\(|0\\rangle\\). For \\(n=0\\) no ket is clean and the statement is vacuous.</p><table class=\"ptp-mods\"><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/Assertions.lean\">Assertions.lean</a></td><td>11 decls</td><td>PTP public specification and assertions (state level)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/Main.lean\">Main.lean</a></td><td>1 decls</td><td>PTP main theorems</td></tr></table>",
