   "summary": "<p class=\"lmeta\">1 module · 32 declarations · 604 lines</p><p>A controlled PTP built by <em>masking</em> one operand. This is not ForShor's construction, which controls every leaf phase; that variant is <strong>not</strong> proved here. On the clean subspace, the control may overlap the other registers in a degenerate way (then the circuit is the identity on the clean span), which the docstring of <code>PTPCtlLowerExactCorrect</code> states.</p><table class=\"ptp-mods\"><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/Controlled.lean\">Controlled.lean</a></td><td>32 decls</td><td>Controlled PTP by operand masking (blueprint item O3, masked-operand form)</td></tr></table>",
