   "role": "O(n^log_k(3k−2)) gates",
   "kind": "ext",
   "summary": "<p class=\"lmeta\">1 module · 25 declarations · 306 lines</p><p>The PTP analogue of ForShor's PhaseProduct gate-count theorem, under the same hypothesis: a <strong>constant policy</strong>, one table at every width. The exponent is \\(\\log_k(3k-2)\\): 2.000 at \\(k=2\\), 1.771 at \\(k=3\\), 1.661 at \\(k=4\\), tending to 1. The count is <code>rz + toffoli + x + h + cnot</code> under <code>shorGateResourceModel</code>, not a T count.</p><table class=\"ptp-mods\"><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/Asymptotic.lean\">Asymptotic.lean</a></td><td>25 decls</td><td>PTP asymptotic gate count (analogue of ForShor `GateCount/PhaseProduct`)</td></tr></table>",
