   "summary": "<p class=\"lmeta\">4 modules · 87 declarations · 887 lines</p><p>Why the theorems are not vacuous, and why the hypotheses are needed. <code>StandardModel</code> specialises the typeclass stack to ForShor's <code>Model.qs</code>. <code>RecursionWitness</code> assembles a concrete \\(k=2\\) gate-level recursion on three 20-qubit registers (child width 14), every structural hypothesis discharged by <code>decide</code>. The <code>Instances/</code> modules are faults: a point-order fault the contract rejects, a width fault (one bit under the exact width, the circuit is wrong on a concrete state). The harness also writes per-policy certificate modules (<code>Instances/PTPSubmitted*.lean</code>) when it checks a policy; those are generated, git-ignored, and not part of the suite's source.</p><table class=\"ptp-mods\"><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/StandardModel.lean\">StandardModel.lean</a></td><td>8 decls</td><td>PTP in ForShor's Standard model (non-vacuity of the typeclass stack)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/RecursionWitness.lean\">RecursionWitness.lean</a></td><td>12 decls</td><td>Non-vacuity of O2: a concrete gate-level recursion</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/Instances/FaultChallenge.lean\">Instances/FaultChallenge.lean</a></td><td>32 decls</td><td>PTP fault challenge: the contract and the width are load-bearing</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/courtneyjzapata/ShorTableOptimization_temp/blob/11fd68b593e5/TableGeneration/RecursiveCost/PTP/Instances/ExactFault.lean\">Instances/ExactFault.lean</a></td><td>35 decls</td><td>O5 fault challenge: one bit below the exact width, the GATE-LEVEL circuit is wrong</td></tr></table>",
